{
  "id": "COMPOUND:919 - PROTEIN:1381",
  "verbalization": "Salicylic acid is implicated in the regulation of Beclin-1 through a multi-step pathway involving 72 kDa type IV collagenase. This enzyme is a target of two distinct compounds, Cryptophycin 23 and N-[(3-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)methyl]-7-methyloctanamide, both of which are linked to salicylic acid. The presence of these intermediates suggests that salicylic acid may influence the activity of these compounds, potentially modulating the downstream effect on Beclin-1. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for salicylic acid in the regulation of autophagy-related proteins, as Beclin-1 is a key component of the autophagic pathway. The evidence supports a mechanism where salicylic acid could act as a modulator of the signaling cascade leading to Beclin-1 activation, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
